Two-Headed Giant (Commander Duels v0.6.2): the rare cards the v0.5.1 card audit left wrong.

Reason: cards whose own code reads one attacking player, one active player or one player's step where
rules 805.4a, 805.8 and 805.10 make it each player of the team's, which the core rules of parts 1, 3
and 7 do not reach. In a team game (Game.getTeammates, from part 1):
- 805.10c, "the attacking player" is one specific attacking player: the controller of the ability
  chooses which (Invasion Plans, Contested Game Ball); "whenever a player (an opponent) attacks"
  triggers for each player of the attacking team who attacks with a creature they control, that
  player being "that attacking player" (Ellie, Brick Master; Emberwilde Captain; Tahngarth, First
  Mate); "you attack" and "they attack you" are the attacks of the creatures each controls (Tenuous
  Truce); Master Warcraft chooses among the attacking team's creatures; War's Toll makes the
  attacking creature's controller's creatures attack, and its controller is told; Territorial
  Hellkite remembers each player's own last combat;
- the watchers of who attacked whom remember the attacking creature's controller, and the
  watchers of "their last turn" forget the turn for each player of the team whose turn it was
  (O-Kagachi, Weathered Sentinels, Arboria's two, Invasion of Fiora's Marchesa);
- Storage Matrix asks each player of the active team during the team's untap step, for the
  permanents they control (805.4b);
- Urabrask's draw replacement replaces the draw of the opponent its trigger was for (805.4d);
- Brine Elemental's "each opponent skips their next untap step" makes a team skip one untap step,
  not one for each of its players (805.8: "If a single effect causes more than one player on the
  same team to ... skip the same step ..., that team ... skips only that step").
docs/engine/two-headed-giant-audit.csv in Commander Duels lists every card reviewed and its verdict.
Every other game type names no teammates, and each change reduces to the card's own code there.
Needs parts 1, 3 and 7.
Upstream: none yet; to be offered to magefree/mage with the other parts.
Remove when: XMage upstream implements Two-Headed Giant, or the format is dropped.

